<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38251" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prēlum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-</span></b> ), i, n.
		premo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a press.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A press-beam</i> for pressing grapes, olives, etc.;
			also, meton., <i>a wine-press</i>, <i>oil-press</i> (class.), <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			31</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cola prelorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 242</span></i>
			 (prela trabes sunt, quibus uva jam calcata premitur, Serv.);
				<i><span class="en">Vitr. 6,
				9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 31, 74, § 317</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Dig.
				19, 2, 19</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A press</i> for smoothing clothes: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tua collucent prela lacernis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					2, 46, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 11, 8, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
